**Result**: draw stage (winner's stage), dark overlay, winner big, text.

Let me now write game logic carefully.

Input:
```js
const keys = new Set();
window.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
  if (['ArrowUp','ArrowDown','ArrowLeft','ArrowRight','Space','Enter','Escape'].includes(e.code)) e.preventDefault();
  if (!e.repeat) handleKey(e.code);
  keys.add(e.code);
  audio.init(); if (audio.pendingTrack) { audio.playTrack(audio.pendingTrack); audio.pendingTrack=null; }
});
window.addEventListener('keyup', e => keys.delete(e.code));
```
But audio.init must happen before playTrack; in keydown call audio.init() then if scene set track. Actually `audio.playTrack` called on scene changes; if ctx not initialized it sets pendingTrack. On first keydown, init then play pending. Implement in initInput:
```js
function ensureAudio(){ audio.init(); if (audio.pendingTrack) { const t=audio.pendingTrack; audio.pendingTrack=null; audio.playTrack(t); } }
```
Call in keydown/pointerdown.

`handleKey(code)`:
- if code==='KeyM' → toggle mute; return.
- if howto overlay → Escape/Enter closes.
- switch scene:
  - title: ArrowUp/Down menu; Enter/Space activate.
  - select: arrows move; Enter lock; Escape back.
  - fight: Escape/KeyP toggle pause.
  - result: arrows, Enter.
- paused: arrows, Enter/Escape.

Note keydown for Enter also adds to keys set; fine.

Menu state: game.menuIndex 0..3.

Title activation:
0: startSelect('cpu')
1: startSelect('local')
2: game.howto=true (from title)
3: cycle difficulty (easy/normal/hard), update label, save? keep in memory.

`startSelect(mode)`:
```js
game.mode=mode;
game.scene='select';
game.select={step:0,cursors:[0,1],picked:[null,null],roulette:0,rouletteIdx:0,cpuPick:null,timer:0};
game.select.cursors=[0, 4]; // p2 default different
game.time=0;
audio.playTrack('menu');
audio.confirm();
```
Default cursor P1 0 (Lemmy), P2 5? For CPU later.

Grid movement:
```js
function moveCursor(idx, dx, dy){
  let col = idx%4, row = Math.floor(idx/4);
  col = (col+dx+4)%4; row = (row+dy+3)%3;
  let n = row*4+col;
  if (n>10) n = 10; // last row has 3
  // if moving right on last row from index 8/9/10, wrap?
  return n;
}
```
Grid last row has indices 8,9,10. Moving down to row 2 col 3 (index 11) invalid → clamp to 10. Moving right from 10 → wraps to 8? Keep simple: if n>10 → n=8? Hmm. Use clamp to 10 for right/down from 10, and left from 8 stays 8? Not critical. Better compute:
```js
let n = row*4+col;
if (n > 10) n = 10;
```
Moving right from 10: col 2→3, n=11→10 stays. Moving left from 8: col 1? 8 is row2 col0; left → col3, n=11→10. Jump to 10. Fine.

Select confirm:
```js
function confirmSelect(){
  const s=game.select;
  if (s.step===0){
    s.picked[0]=s.cursors[0]; audio.confirm();
    if (game.mode==='cpu'){ s.step=2; s.roulette=0; s.rouletteIdx=0; }
    else { s.step=1; s.cursors[1]= (s.cursors[0]+1)%11; }
  } else if (s.step===1){
    s.picked[1]=s.cursors[1]; audio.confirm(); beginMatch();
  }
}
```
During step 2 (CPU roulette), update in select update: every 4 frames change rouletteIdx random; after 55 frames lock random and begin match. Maybe use weighted pick? Random index. Exclude same? Mirror allowed but CPU picking same char is less interesting; pick random from other 10. Do that.

In select update, `s.rouletteT++`; at 50 lock.

Also if step 2, pressing Enter could skip? Let it play.

`beginMatch()`:
```js
game.scene='fight';
game.stage = pickStage();
game.round=1; game.roundWins=[0,0];
game.fighters=[makeFighter(picked[0],0,150), makeFighter(picked[1],1,330)];
game.projectiles=[]; particles=[]; floats=[]; afterimages=[];
game.paused=false; game.result=null; game.time=0;
startRound(true);
audio.playTrack('fight');
```
pickStage: char stages; if equal use it else random.

`startRound(first)`:
```js
const f1=game.fighters[0], f2=...;
const positions = [150,330];
for each: reset...
f1.hp=f1.maxHp...; f1.meter preserved (if !first)
f1.roundsWon = game.roundWins[i]? store on fighter.
```
Simpler: keep roundsWon on fighters and reset only positions/health. Initialize at match start. Round wins increment on KO.

`game.roundWins` not needed separately; use fighters[i].roundsWon. Result uses them.

Reset:
```js
f.x = i===0?150:330; f.y=GROUND; f.vx=f.vy=0; f.facing=i===0?1:-1; f.hp=f.maxHp; f.hpDisplay=f.maxHp; f.state='idle'; f.onGround=true; f.attack=null; f.hitstun=0; f.blockstun=0; f.crouching=false; f.blocking=false; f.koT=0; f.combo=0; f.comboTimer=0; f.invuln=60;
```
Invuln 60? During intro, no attacks anyway. Set 0.

Meter preserved across rounds, but at match start 0. At first round set 0. Keep as is (new fighters start 0).

Timer: 60*60 = 3600 frames.

Announce system:
`game.announce = {text, sub, t:0, dur, size, color}`. Update increments t in update. Draw only if t<dur. Use fade.

Intro: fightLock=100. During fightLock decrement. At 40 show FIGHT. Unlock at 0. So ROUND shown 60 frames then FIGHT 40.

Let me set fightLock=95; at 38 announce FIGHT (dur 45), unlock at 0. Good.

KO round over: after roundOverT reaches 110 → next round or result. During this, announce "K.O." displayed with dur 90. On next round, announce replaced.

Result condition: winner.roundsWon >= 2.

`endMatch(winner)`:
```js
game.scene='result';
game.result={winnerIdx: winner.player, winner, loser, rounds:[f1.roundsWon,f2.roundsWon], perfect: winner.hp>=winner.maxHp, stage: game.stage};
audio.stopTrack(); audio.fanfare();
game.resultT=0; game.resultIndex=0;
```
Note winner.hp after KO of opponent = winner's remaining HP. Perfect if winner.hp===maxHp (no damage taken across the match? Just final round). Fine.

Result buttons: REMATCH, CHARACTERS, TITLE.
- Rematch: rebuild fighters with same picks, start match.
- Characters: startSelect(game.mode).
- Title: scene='title', audio menu.

Result screen uses result.winner char.

**Time up**:
```js
function timeUp(){
  game.roundOver=true; game.roundOverT=0; game.roundResult='time';
  audio.timeUp();
  const f1=game.fighters[0], f2=game.fighters[1];
  if (f1.hp===f2.hp){
    game.announce={text:'DRAW',...};
    game.koWinner=null;
  } else {
    const w = f1.hp>f2.hp?f1:f2; const l = w===f1?f2:f1;
    w.roundsWon++;
    l.hp=0; l.state='ko'; l.koT=0; l.vx=-l.facing*2; l.vy=-3; l.onGround=false;
    game.koWinner=w;
    game.announce={text:'TIME UP',...};
  }
  game.hitstop=10; game.shake=6;
}
```
After roundOverT 110: if draw → next round (no result). Else if winner rounds>=2 → result. Otherwise next round.

`game.roundOver` prevents input; timer stops.

**updateFighter** details. I'll implement carefully with game.roundOver handling.

Also if `game.paused` skip all.

**Hit detection** must not hit during intro (fightLock>0). Check in resolveAttack: if fightLock>0 return.

**Projectile**: update only when not roundOver? Let existing projectiles fly and hit even after KO? Stop on roundOver. Clear on startRound.

**Meter display**: f.meterDisplay += (meter - display)*0.15.

**HP display**: lerp toward hp at 0.08 per frame (slow drain).

**Screen shake**: set game.shake on hit; decay `game.shake *= 0.9`; render offset random within shake. Use deterministic-ish random fine.

**Hitstop**: decrement at start of updateFight, but still update particles/floats/shake/announce. Also hpDisplay lerp.

**Slowmo** on KO: we can just use hitstop 16 and then normal. Skip slowmo complexity.

**Particles**:
```js
function spawnParticles(x,y,color,count,opts={}) {
 for i: particles.push({x,y,vx:cos*sp,vy:sin*sp,life:...,size:1..3,color,grav:0.1})
}
```
Update particles: x+=vx, y+=vy, vy+=grav, life--; remove when life<=0. Render as rects, alpha = life/maxLife.

**Floats** (damage numbers): {x,y,text,color,life,vy:-0.6}. Draw with pixel font scale 1 or 2.

**Afterimages**: store {x,y,facing,char,animT,state,attack?} and life; render with globalAlpha. Since drawFighter needs many fields, store snapshot of f relevant fields:
```js
{char, x, y, facing, state, animT, onGround, crouching, blocking, hitstun, attack}
```
Draw with alpha 0.25 and color? Can't tint easily. Use alpha 0.2. Add for special dash only.

**Projectile rendering**:
```js
function drawProjectile(p, t){
  const {x,y,color,style,super:p.super} = p;
  ctx.save(); ctx.globalAlpha=0.9;
  // glow
  ctx.globalAlpha=0.18; ell(ctx,x,y,r*1.6,r*1.6,color);
  if style==='laser' or 'beam': draw elongated capsule: px(x-r*1.5, y-r*0.4, r*3, r*0.8, color), white core.
  else if 'claw': draw claw-ish arc
  else if 'star': starPath
  else if 'ink': blob with drips
  else: bubble circle with white ring.
  trail particles spawned in update.
  ctx.restore();
}
```
Use ell/px from local helpers (define in game.js or export from sprites? I'll define small helpers in game.js).

Projectile trail: every 2 frames spawn particle at p.x,p.y with color alpha.

**HUD** as planned.

**Announcer**: draw big text with outline. Add sub text.

**Fight scene pause**:
`game.paused` toggled; when paused, still render; overlay panel with options. Pause options: RESUME, RESTART ROUND, QUIT. Keyboard nav via game.pauseIndex. On restart round: startRound() resets current round (doesn't reset round wins). On quit: scene title.

Also if paused, audio keeps playing; maybe reduce volume? Not necessary.

**Touch controls**:
- HTML buttons with data-act.
- JS: pointerdown → setTouch(act,true) + ensureAudio; pointerup/cancel/leave → false. Prevent default.
- Need to hide when scene !== fight or paused? Keep visible during fight. Add class 'show' on #touch-controls.
- Also pause button sets paused.
- For menus, canvas clicks.

The canvas pointer handler:
```js
canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e=>{
  ensureAudio();
  const rect=canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
  const x=(e.clientX-rect.left)/rect.width*W;
  const y=(e.clientY-rect.top)/rect.height*H;
  handleClick(x,y);
});
```
Also pointermove for hover.

For touch buttons, use separate elements so canvas doesn't receive. Overlay covers screen but pointer-events none except buttons.

**Mute button**: HTML button toggles audio. Update text.

**Resize**: set canvas style width/height fit. Also account for devicePixelRatio? Backing store fixed 480x270; CSS scaling up. Good.

**Scene update loop**:
```js
let last=performance.now(), acc=0;
function frame(now){
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  const dt = Math.min(50, now-last); last=now; acc+=dt;
  let steps=0;
  while(acc>=1000/60 && steps<4){ step(); acc-=1000/60; steps++; }
  render();
}
```
Step:
```js
game.time++;
if (game.scene==='fight' && !game.paused) updateFight();
else if (game.scene==='select') updateSelect();
else if (game.scene==='title') updateTitle(); // embers
else if (game.scene==='result') updateResult();
```
Announce updates in fight.

Title update just time.

Select update: roulette; also animate preview.

Result update: confetti spawn, winner hop.

**Render**:
```js
ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=false;
ctx.clearRect? fill background each scene.
switch scene.
```
Set canvas background black.

For fight: draw stage, shadows, fighters, projectiles, particles, afterimages, floats, then HUD/announce. Apply shake to world only.

Ordering: projectiles behind fighters? Some in front. Draw projectiles before fighters for glow behind, and front? Just draw after fighters so visible.

Fighters draw with `drawFighter(ctx, f.char, f)`. For KO, f.state 'ko' and koT.

Win state: winner.state='win'; drawFighter pose win. Ensure poseOf handles state win (yes, p.win).

