Now register buffered presses on keydown and touch. Add a reverse mapping and function. Place near input helpers.

For keydown, after ensureAudio and if !e.repeat. We need to buffer before onKeyDown? It only matters during fight. Do:

```
const BUFFER_ACTIONS = new Set(['up','punch','kick','special']);
function bufferKey(code) {
  for (let p = 0; p < 2; p++) {
    const map = p === 0 ? P1_KEYS : P2_KEYS;
    for (const a of BUFFER_ACTIONS) {
      if (map[a].includes(code)) bufferPress(p, a);
    }
  }
}
```

Call in keydown listener when !e.repeat. Also on touch press for key in set.

Clear buffers on startRound? Actually clearing in startSelect/beginMatch/startRound. Simpler: clear in beginMatch and startRound called. Add clearBuffers() in startRound call? startRound is imported; we call it in pause resume. We can add clearBuffers in beginMatch and in step when scene changes? Not necessary but good: clear on beginMatch, quitToTitle, startSelect. Also when paused, step returns early; buffers could linger. If paused for long then resume, buffered tap could fire. Clear when pausing and unpausing. Let's add clearBuffers() in onKeyDown pause enter and handlePauseKey resume, plus beginMatch/startSelect/quitToTitle.

Actually simpler: tickBuffers only during fight and not paused. If paused, buffers retain. On unpause, could fire stale action. Add clearBuffers() when setting paused true/false.

Let me add the mapping and calls.

